#. §15: `rcases`
#: Game.Levels.ArgWorld.arg_docs
msgid "The §0 tactic is used bring new (and provable) assumptions into the proof state. It can also be used to desctructure existing assumptions.\n"
"### Basic Usage ###\n"
"The most basic usage of the §1 tactic might look like the following:\n"
"§2\n"
"where §3 is the name you want to give (or *identifier*) for the proposition you wish to bring into the proof-state, and §4 is a (short) proof of that proposition. In some cases, you may wish to explicitly provide the form of the proposition being brought in:\n"
"§5\n"
"where §6 is the form of the proposition. This is helpful if §7 is definitionally equivalent to the proposition whose §8 is provided.\n"
"\n"
"### Opening a New Goal###\n"
"If the proof of the proposition you wish to bring into the proof-state requires the use of tactics, you can use the §9 tactic to open a new goal in which those tactics can be applied. For example:\n"
"§10\n"
"will create a new goal whose target is §11.\n"
"\n"
"### Advanced Usage ###\n"
"The §12 tactic can simultaneously destructure those propositions brought into the proof-state as assumptions. Typical usage looks like:\n"
"§13\n"
"where §14 is a pattern as in the tactic §15."
msgstr ""

